Tavletta for Debian
===================

Printers on USB
---------------

The package installs a udev rule (/usr/lib/udev/rules.d/70-tavletta.rules)
that lets the user at the computer, in an active local session, use the
USB label printers of the makers Tavletta recognises by name: Brother, cab,
DYMO, TSC and Zebra (/dev/usb/lp*), and NIIMBOT printers (a USB serial
port, /dev/ttyACM*, vendor 3513). It takes effect when the printer is
plugged in again. Printers of other makers that Tavletta drives by their
command set (ESC/POS, EPL, TSPL), and users who print from elsewhere (an
SSH session, a service), need the group lp, for NIIMBOT printers dialout:

  sudo usermod -aG lp,dialout USER

The print server
----------------

The print server as a system service is in the package tavletta-server.
